      'The orbit is the bony socket that holds and protects the eye. It is shaped like a pyramid lying on its side, with its base at the front, the opening we see on the skull, and its apex at the back, pointing towards the middle of the skull. Seven bones contribute to its walls, and some of these walls are extremely thin.',
