      'The nasal cavity runs from the nostrils at the front to the nasopharynx at the back and is divided by the septum into two halves. Its job is to prepare the air we breathe for the lungs: it warms it, adds moisture and traps dust and microbes on sticky mucus, which tiny hairs (cilia) then sweep back to the throat to be swallowed. It also contains the organ of smell.',
