      'The labyrinth is a tube within a tube. The outer bony labyrinth is a set of channels in the bone, filled with a fluid called perilymph. Floating inside it is the membranous labyrinth, a set of soft tubes filled with a different fluid, endolymph, which contains the sensory cells. These cells have tiny hairs on their surface that bend when the fluid moves, which opens channels and generates nerve signals.',
